# k.procedures/shards/compose: 5 compositions by the book (block "15:00" item 3): a story (k.story), a presentation, an essay, a scientific article about a topic and a report of what was done, each a genre of k.genres written as a w.document; their choices are `choose` bindings solved jointly under their matches and sampled by k.interest (the format addition proposed in questions.md Q57).
# sources: hand-core 1 (hand-written in this repository: tools/procedures-core.mjs)
# license: CC0-1.0
# script: tools/procedures-core.mjs

# write a story
@k.procedures.method.write_a_story k.procedures.method name="write a story" about="A story by the book (k.story, the genre \"story\" of k.genres): choose together a goal, an obstacle that blocks it, a setting that has the obstacle, the means that overcomes it, the act that uses the means, a helper who has the means, a protagonist who can have the goal and lacks the means, one to three attempts that fail, and the target of the goal; then make the document and one chapter per part of the genre. Each element of k.story is the binding of its name (turning point: turning_point); std.compose tells it in its part with its move." act=make world=w.document example="write a story" example="tell me a story" core.source="hand-core 1"
